---
// Public summary of docs/privacy.md; update both together.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';

const lastUpdated = 'November 5, 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site handles your personal data.">
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This site is a personal website. It does not use cookies, does not store anything on your device, does not run
      analytics, and does not load resources from third-party services. This page explains the little data that is
      still processed when you visit it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {profile.name}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>, is the data controller for this
      site.
    </p>

    <h2>What data is processed</h2>
    <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
    <p>
      Like any website, the servers that deliver these pages receive your IP address, browser user agent, and the page
      you request. This happens through the hosting providers:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>alexkander.github.io</strong> is hosted by GitHub, Inc., which may keep server logs for security purposes.
        See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>alexkander.dev</strong> is self-hosted and delivered through Cloudflare, Inc. My own server logs are kept
        for a maximum of 14 days. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data is used only to deliver the site and keep it secure. The legal basis is my legitimate interest in
      operating a functional and secure website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </p>

    <h3>When you email me</h3>
    <p>
      If you write to me, I receive your email address, your name if you include it, and your message. I use them only
      to reply, based on your request (Article 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR), and keep them only as long as the conversation
      requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not set cookies or use any other form of storage on your device, and it does not use analytics or
      tracking tools. If that changes, this page will be updated before it does.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub and Cloudflare are based in the United States. Transfers of your data to them rely on the EU-US Data
      Privacy Framework, under which both companies are certified.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to access, correct, or delete your personal data, restrict or object to its processing, or receive it
      in a portable format. Email <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> and I will reply within one
      month. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in
      the country where you live or work.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy is updated whenever the site starts processing data in a new way. The date at the top shows the latest
      version.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
